# Git Commit Rule

After completing a set of related edits, always create a git commit with a clear, descriptive message.

- Commit when a logical unit of work is done (feature, fix, refactor)
- Use conventional commit style: `type(scope): message` (e.g. `fix(woo): add stock quantity to product API`)
- Keep commits focused; avoid mixing unrelated changes
